# Frontend Rules

Before generating code, read:

- docs/PROJECT_RULES.md
- docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md
- docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md

Do not violate these documents.

---

# Objective

Build a premium, calm, luxurious retreat website.

The website should feel inspired by:

- OnlyHotel
- Aman Resorts
- Six Senses
- Apple
- Notion

Do NOT copy layouts.

Only follow their design philosophy.

---

# Design Philosophy

Every page should feel:

- Calm
- Spacious
- Elegant
- Premium
- Natural

Avoid:

- Busy layouts
- Bright colours
- Heavy shadows
- Flashy animations
- Corporate appearance

Whitespace is part of the design.

---

# Layout Rules

Every page should follow:

Navbar

↓

Hero

↓

Content Sections

↓

CTA

↓

Footer

Unless the page has a special layout.

---

# Typography

Heading

Cormorant Garamond

Body

Manrope

Labels

Inter

Maintain typography hierarchy.

Never invent new font sizes.

---

# Colour Rules

Always use colours from DESIGN_SYSTEM.md.

Never hardcode hex colours.

Use CSS variables.

---

# Components

Prefer existing shared components.

Reuse:

Container

Section

SectionTitle

PageHeader

Button

Card

ImageCard

CTA

GalleryGrid

QuoteBlock

Never duplicate components.

---

# Tailwind Rules

Use TailwindCSS only.

No inline styles.

No CSS modules.

No styled-components.

---

# Images

Use next/image.

Always provide:

alt

width

height

priority only for hero images

Use Cloudinary URLs when images come from CMS.

---

# Buttons

Use shadcn/ui Button.

Allowed variants:

Primary

Secondary

Outline

Ghost

Danger

Do not create custom button implementations.

---

# Forms

Use:

React Hook Form

Zod

shadcn/ui form components

Every form must include:

Loading state

Validation

Error messages

Success feedback

---

# Animations

Use Framer Motion only.

Allowed:

Fade

Slide

Scale

Reveal

Parallax

Hover

Avoid:

Bounce

Rotate

Elastic

Continuous animation

Animation should support usability.

---

# Responsive Rules

Desktop first.

Support:

Desktop

Laptop

Tablet

Mobile

Never allow horizontal scrolling.

Maintain spacing consistency.

---

# Accessibility

Use semantic HTML.

Provide:

Alt text

Labels

Keyboard navigation

Visible focus state

ARIA attributes where required.

---

# Performance

Prefer Server Components.

Only use Client Components for:

Forms

Animations

Dialogs

Search

Interactive UI

Use lazy loading when appropriate.

Optimise images.

---

# SEO

Use Next.js Metadata API.

Every public page should have:

Title

Description

Open Graph image (future-ready)

Canonical URL support

Do not install external SEO libraries.

---

# Code Quality

Keep components under ~200 lines when practical.

Extract reusable logic.

Avoid duplicated JSX.

Use descriptive names.

Avoid deeply nested components.

---

# Never Do

Do not redesign existing UI without instruction.

Do not change global colours.

Do not create new spacing systems.

Do not introduce new component libraries.

Do not use Bootstrap.

Do not use Material UI.

Do not hardcode website content.

Do not duplicate existing components.

---

# Final Rule

Every page should feel like it belongs to the same premium product.

Consistency is more important than creativity.

When in doubt, reuse existing patterns.